From dccf2f39a0e7c203730b1d6cc05dcd143d4055f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taekim <taekim@day34.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 02:50:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 01/39] feat(ffi): structured JSON export + LaTeX equation
 emitter for FastDocReader
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FastDocReader consumes HWP through this fork's C FFI, so anything the
reader needs to render must cross that boundary as data. Upstream's
export dropped four facts the reader cannot recover on its own:
paragraph style names (Korean HWP files carry headings as user-named
styles, not outline levels — without them a document renders flat with
no table of contents), image alignment, and the image width criterion
that says what a relative width is a percentage OF.

Equations are emitted as LaTeX so the reader can hand them to its
existing formula engine instead of growing a second one.

Committing this locally because the working tree was the only copy —
a rebuild of the vendored static library would otherwise have silently
reverted the reader to upstream's narrower export.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
